{"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"],"title":"Creating a Schedule","anchor":"Creating-a-Schedule"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)"],"title":"Running Systems","anchor":"Running-Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/after(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/before(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/inSet(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguous(with:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runIf(_:)"],"title":"Ordering and Conditioning Every System","anchor":"Ordering-and-Conditioning-Every-System"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)"],"title":"Inspecting a Schedule","anchor":"Inspecting-a-Schedule"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"Schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L96"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"text":", which runs each system once:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Ordering-Systems","level":3,"text":"Ordering Systems"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or before one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written earlier, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its written place:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to throw","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","level":3,"text":"Running Systems at the Same Time"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, and the world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/names":{"abstract":[{"text":"The names of the schedule’s systems’ types, in the order the systems run.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","title":"names","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/names","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"names","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/writeDOT(to:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","title":"writeDOT(to:)","